{{also|kartoffel}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From older {{m|de|Tartuffel}} or {{m|de|Tartüffel}} ({{C.|18}}), from {{der|de|it|tartufolo}}, diminutive of {{m|it|tartufo||truffle}}, from {{der|de|ML.|*territūberum}} or {{der|de|la|[[terrae]] [[tūber]]||tuber of the earth}}.

The use as an ethnic nickname is due to the prominence of potatoes in German cuisine. Compare {{m|de|Spaghetti|t=Italian}}, {{m|de|Käskopp|t=Dutch person}}.

